---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import WorkRow from '../components/WorkRow.astro';
import WorkImage from '../components/WorkImage.astro';

import politics from '../assets/images/editorial_politics.png';
import culture from '../assets/images/editorial_culture.png';
import tatler from '../assets/images/editorial_tatler.png';
import smile from '../assets/images/editorial_smile.png';

const imgSizes = '(max-width: 760px) 92vw, 620px';
const imgWidths = [480, 800, 1240];
const imgQuality = 90;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Editorial Work — Miguel Escobar"
  description="Selected editorial work by Miguel Escobar — features and reporting for Esquire Philippines, Tatler Asia, and Smile Magazine."
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <section class="page-title" data-reveal>
      <h1>Editorial Work</h1>
    </section>

    <WorkRow>
      <Fragment slot="text">
        <h2>Politics in Esquire</h2>
        <p>
          In my time with Esquire, I produced and published features on politicians and politically
          controversial figures. These include former presidential spokesperson <a
            href="https://www.esquiremag.ph/long-reads/esqa/salvador-panelo-a1513-a1521-20160919-lfrm3"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener">Salvador Panelo</a>, former senator <a
            href="https://www.esquiremag.ph/long-reads/what-ive-learned/richard-gordon-what-i-ve-learned-a00207-20170717-lfrm"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener">Dick Gordon</a>, and political influencer <a
            href="https://www.esquiremag.ph/long-reads/profiles/mocha-uson-full-text-a1521-20161202-lfrm4"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener">Mocha Uson</a>. I also worked on Esquire’s blockbuster December 2016 issue, featuring <a
            href="https://www.esquiremag.ph/long-reads/profiles/her-excellency-full-text-a1506-20180402-lfrm3"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener">Vice President Leni Robredo</a> on the cover.
        </p>
        <p>With Esquire, I was on the frontlines of online culture wars, just as social media’s era of political rancour and polarisation began in the Philippines. So through my work, I learned firsthand about the roles and responsibilities of media in a democracy.</p>
      </Fragment>
      <WorkImage
        slot="media"
        image={politics}
        alt="Portrait of former Philippine Vice President Leni Robredo in a red top against a dark background, from Esquire Philippines."
        ratio="4 / 3"
        sizes={imgSizes}
        widths={imgWidths}
        quality={imgQuality}
      />
    </WorkRow>

    <WorkRow>
      <Fragment slot="text">
        <h2>Culture in Esquire</h2>
        <p>
          Politics and current events were just among many areas we covered at Esquire. I also got to write and produce features in style and entertainment, including <a
            href="https://www.esquiremag.ph/life/women/anne-curtis-smith-is-a-woman-we-love-a00207-20171111"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener">big celebrity interviews</a>, <a
            href="https://www.esquiremag.ph/culture/movies-and-tv/goyo-cinematographer-pong-ignacio-frame-epic-a00203-20180910-lfrm"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener">film and cinema stories</a>, and <a
            href="https://www.esquiremag.ph/style/fashion/local-denimheads-have-produced-the-first-filipino-made-raw-selvedge-jeans-a00207-20171024-lfrm2"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener">fashion features</a>.</p>
        <p>
          I wrote and produced one of Esquire’s biggest-ever stories: <a
            href="https://www.esquiremag.ph/long-reads/what-ive-learned/eddie-garcia-what-ive-learned-a1513-20181015-lfrm"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener">an interview with Eddie Garcia</a>, a legendary actor and icon of Filipino cinema. <a
            href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yY4LLYrMHt8"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener">The full interview</a> is still the publication’s most-viewed video on Facebook and YouTube.
        </p>
      </Fragment>
      <WorkImage
        slot="media"
        image={culture}
        alt="A dramatic, low-key editorial close-up portrait of actor Eddie Garcia in a pinstriped suit against a dark background, from a feature in Esquire Philippines."
        ratio="4 / 3"
        sizes={imgSizes}
        widths={imgWidths}
        quality={imgQuality}
      />
    </WorkRow>

    <WorkRow>
      <Fragment slot="text">
        <h2>Tatler Asia’s Most Influential</h2>
        <p>
          Asia’s Most Influential is one of Tatler Asia’s signature editorial products. Every year,
          Tatler publishes a list of profiles of over 500 influential people from various fields. In
          2021 <a
            href="https://www.tatlerasia.com/power-purpose/ideas-education/art-influence-and-the-purveyors-responsibility-according-to-top-auctioneer-jonathan-crockett"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener">I contributed</a> over 100 of those profiles, including honourees in Singapore
          and the Philippines. It was, for me, a writing exercise that demanded quick writing and
          fast-turnaround fact-checking.
        </p>
      </Fragment>
      <WorkImage
        slot="media"
        image={tatler}
        alt="Tatler’s “Asia’s Most Influential” series title, set in white and gold serif lettering on black."
        ratio="4 / 3"
        sizes={imgSizes}
        widths={imgWidths}
        quality={imgQuality}
      />
    </WorkRow>

    <WorkRow last>
      <Fragment slot="text">
        <h2>Smile Magazine Cover Story</h2>
        <p>
          I wrote the cover story for <a
            href="https://smile.ink-live.com/html5/reader/production/default.aspx?pubname=&amp;edid=029443cb-cf76-46cf-a91b-5360ee2806f0"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener">the February 2020 issue</a> of Cebu Pacific Air’s in-flight magazine, Smile.
          It was a feature on Barotac Nuevo, Iloilo, the one and only town in the entire Philippines that loves football
          more than basketball.
        </p>
      </Fragment>
      <WorkImage
        slot="media"
        image={smile}
        alt="A football match on the town plaza pitch in front of the historic Barotac Nuevo church in Iloilo, for the Smile magazine cover story."
        ratio="4 / 3"
        sizes={imgSizes}
        widths={imgWidths}
        quality={imgQuality}
      />
    </WorkRow>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-title {
    padding: clamp(36px, 7vh, 80px) 0 clamp(24px, 3vw, 40px);
  }
  .page-title h1 {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-synthesis: none;
    font-size: clamp(44px, 6.8vw, 96px);
    letter-spacing: -0.008em;
  }
</style>
